### VS Code REST Client (extension humao.rest-client). Start the server first: npm run dev
@base = http://localhost:3000

### Register -> 201
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "correct horse 42" }

### Duplicate email -> 409
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "Alice@Example.com", "password": "correct horse 42" }

### Weak password -> 400 with details
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@example.com", "password": "short" }

### Login -> 200 { token }; the token is stored in a variable for the requests below
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "correct horse 42" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Wrong password -> 401
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "wrong password" }

### Current user -> 200
GET {{base}}/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### No token -> 401
GET {{base}}/profile

### Create a diagram, the owner is the caller -> 201
POST {{base}}/diagrams
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "title": "Login flow", "notation": "UML", "sourceCode": "user -> server", "priority": "low" }

### List diagrams -> 200
GET {{base}}/diagrams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Somebody else's diagram -> 403 (replace 1 with an id owned by another user)
DELETE {{base}}/diagrams/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin only: regular user -> 403
GET {{base}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
